   "exec_error": null,
   "is_refusal": false,
   "output": "In accordance with *Graham v. John Deere* and *KSR v. Teleflex*, Applicant respectfully traverses the 35 U.S.C. 103 rejection of claim 1 over Lee in view of Garcia. \n\nFirst, the cited combination fails to disclose or suggest all limitations of claim 1. Specifically, while Lee teaches fine-tuning with standard loss functions, neither Lee nor Garcia teaches or suggests \"fine-tuning the neural network using cluster-specific loss functions,\" as expressly recited in claim 1. \n\nSecond, the Examiner asserts a motivation to combine Lee and Garcia based on improving training efficiency because both references relate to organizing data representations. However, this rationale is impermissibly speculative and amounts to hindsight reconstruction. The Office Action excerpt fails to explain why one of ordinary skill in the art would have looked to Garcia's recommendation system context to modify Lee\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s neural network training method. Garcia\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s application to recommendation systems is distinct from Lee\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s contrastive learning framework, and the cited excerpt provides no factual foundation establishing how combining hierarchical clustering of feature vectors with Lee's architecture would successfully achieve the claimed cluster-specific loss function fine-tuning. \n\nTherefore, the Examiner has failed to establish a prima facie case of obviousness. Reconsideration and withdrawal of the rejection of claim 1 are requested.",
